<title>FRANCE: French Aug trade surplus hits record 13.89 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>French Aug trade surplus hits record 13.89 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>France had a record seasonally adjusted trade surplus in August of 13.89 billion francs compared with a revised surplus in July of 10.40 billion, provisional customs office data showed.</p>
<p>The office had originally reported a surplus in July of 11.10 billion francs.</p>
<p>Detailed figures, in billions of francs and seasonally adjusted unless otherwise stated, were as follows:</p>
<p>					   Aug     July</p>
<p> Trade balance			13.89    10.40</p>
<p> Trade balance (unadjusted)	7.93    12.80</p>
<p> Imports			     111.15   110.72</p>
<p> Exports			     125.04   121.12</p>
<p> Agri-business balance	     5.44     4.49</p>
<p> Energy balance		     -5.11    -5.75</p>
<p> Industrial/military balance     9.48     7.67</p>
<p> Airbus exports	 2.14 (6  planes)  1.73 (5)</p>
<p> Defence (unadj)		     2.18    0.69</p>
<p> Unadjusted exports		 92.07  126.22</p>
<p> Unadjusted imports		 84.15  113.42</p>
<p> European Union			2.62    3.73</p>
<p> Germany				 1.25    0.92</p>
<p> Japan				  -1.48   -1.41</p>
<p> United States			 0.026  -2.26</p>
<p>Cumulative figures for the first seven months of the year were as follows:</p>
<p>				     Jan-Aug 1996     Jan-Aug 1995</p>
<p> Before seasonal adjustment     77.11		64.95</p>
<p> Seasonally adjusted		77.53		65.39</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 42 21 53 81</p>
